{
  "dom_id": "step-q177452",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "$\\sqrt{5}$ is rational, **or** $3|12$ **and** $3|18.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P:\\sqrt{5}\\text{ is rational}$\n\n- $Q:3|12$\n\n- $R:3|18\\text{ }$",
  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $\\sqrt{5}$ is rational. This corresponds to $P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $3|12$ and $3|18.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{3|12}_{⏟}}_{Q}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{3|18}_{⏟}}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $Q∧R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{\\sqrt{5}\\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{3|12\\text{ and }3|18}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∧\\,R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∨(Q∧R).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
